<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21492" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illaudātus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inl-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not praised</i>, <i>unpraised</i>, <i>without fame</i>, <i>obscure.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gubernator illaudatus, inglorius subit portum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 9, 26, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 11, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 14,
				632</span></i>; Claud. ap. <i><span class="en">Ruf. 2,
			225</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b> for illaudabilis, <i>unworthy of praise</i>, <i>blamable</i>, <i>detestable</i>, = abominandus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Busiris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. G.
					3, 5</span></i>
			 Serv.; cf. <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 6, 17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
